 # Transfer Function and Shading Techniques
 ## Overview
-This family defines the optical properties (color and opacity) and illumination models applied to samples in direct volume ray casting, enabling the selective visualization of internal structures and realistic depth perception . It differs from [Programmable Transfer Function DVR](8220-programmable-transfer-function-dvr.md) by focusing on the material property assignment and lighting calculation rather than the computational optimization of the transfer function lookup, and from [Lighting and Shading Techniques](8281-lighting-and-shading-techniques.md) by encompassing specific implementations like Phong illumination and stylized cel shading .
+This family encompasses methods that define the optical properties (color and opacity) of volume data via transfer functions and enhance visual realism through shading models. It differs from [Direct volume ray casting](19-direct-volume-ray-casting.md) by providing the specific mechanisms for $T(V) \rightarrow (\mathbf{c}, \alpha)$ mapping and illumination calculation, and from [Classified Volume Rendering](3590-classified-volume-rendering.md) by supporting continuous, multi-dimensional opacity definitions rather than discrete class assignments.
 ## Shared principles
