-## Sources+The integration of transfer functions and shading into direct volume rendering evolved from the need to overcome the "fuzzy" appearance of early DVR methods. Early work by Levoy  established the foundational ray-casting framework. The introduction of Phong shading to volumes allowed for better depth perception . Programmable transfer functions emerged with the advent of GPU shaders, enabling real-time interaction . Cel shading for volumes was introduced to provide stylized visualization options .
